## 🔁 How Hard Is This To Change?

Not bad at all — it’s mostly **query updates**, not logic rewrites:

* Your `$wpdb->get_results()` for invoices just needs to **JOIN** to the bridge tables.
* Your existing class methods (`AYS_Invoices`, `AYS_Payments`, etc.) can stay the same, just add optional JOINs or helper methods like:

  ```php
  AYS_Invoices::get_services($invoice_id);
  AYS_Clients::get_service_types($client_id);
  ```
* Back-end UI only needs one multi-select dropdown for “Services” when creating invoices.

So you’re not losing code — just tightening relationships.

